  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe Story of the Oxfordshire Yeomanry – Queen’s Own Oxfordshire Hussars 1798-1998\n£7.95\n\nSorry, this item is out of stock\n\n \n\nCommissioned by The Oxfordshire Yeomanry Trust, this book documents the history of the county Yeomanry from 1798-1998. Including information on its origins and function, as well as the campaigns and battles it has been involved in, from the Boer War to the Second World War and beyond.\n\nWritten by David Eddershaw.\n\nContents\n\n1: Origins\n\n2: In Support of the Civil Power\n\n21: “The Queen’s Own”\n\n39: The Boer War and Beyond, 1899-1913\n\n51: Flanders, 1914-1918\n\n61: Territorial Artillery Between the Wars\n\n69: The Second World War\n\n77: The Yeomanry Since the War\n\n85: Index\n\nPaperback, 88 pages.\n\nISBN 0-9534694-0-9\n\n \n\nRelated products\nBugle & Sabre VII\n£5.00 Add to cart\nHistory of the 43rd and 52nd (Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire) Light Infantry in the Great War 1914-1918 Volume II The 52nd Light Infantry in France and Belgium\n£30.00 Add to cart\nBritish Army Cap Badges of the First World War\n£14.99 Add to cart\nThe Skipper’s War: Dragon School, Oxford & The Great War\n£20.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
